[32m+[m[32m## Phase 8 — Backup & Restore[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPhase 8 is implemented in the working tree and is awaiting final testing and commit. Administrators can create, verify, list, and restore local backups from the Backup & restore screen. A backup is a portable ZIP archive stored under the application-data `backups/` directory. It contains a SQLite snapshot at `database/documents.db`, every managed document under `storage/`, and a `manifest.json` with SHA-256 hashes and sizes for each included file. Backup creation verifies the archive before marking it verified.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRestore validates the ZIP structure, rejects unsafe paths, verifies every manifest hash, stages the contents, preserves the current database and storage while installing the restored pair, and rolls back the filesystem swap when installation fails. Restore and verification are administrator-only Tauri commands. Backup history is stored in the `backup_history` table and is bounded to the newest 100 records in the UI. The backup archive itself is portable and can be copied to another compatible application-data backup location; it contains no plaintext export of passwords beyond the database’s existing Argon2 hashes.[m
